#  Build output.
#
#  These are directory patterns rather than a list per crate, so a crate
#  added later is covered without editing this file. Every project file in
#  the repository declares Object_Dir and Exec_Dir inside its own crate, so
#  build output only ever appears in one of these.
obj/
lib/
bin/
alire/
config/
docs/api/
docs/gnatdoc/

#  The virtual machine image, the guest's staging directory, and anything
#  else built for an environment other than the host.
/build/

#  Conventional Ada and object-file leftovers. Note that these are a
#  convenience for keeping `git status` readable, not the defence against a
#  build escaping its object directory — scripts/check-tree-clean.sh is,
#  and it runs as part of ./scripts/test.sh. Two of the file kinds a stray
#  build produces are Ada source by extension, so no pattern here would
#  catch them anyway.
*.ali
*.o
*.a
*.dSYM/
